"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record for Tuscola County runs from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids September to October came in under 90% of normal in 34 of 75 years. In 2025, January to February came in at 63% of normal and August to September at 78% on the middle of the grids. In 2026 so far, March to April came in at 217% of normal on the middle of the grids. Grid 27786 had its driest year in 1963 at 60%.</p>"}
